WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.491
Security teams rely heavily on alerts generated by SIEMs, EDR platforms, firewalls, and other security technologies.

2
00:00:08.491 --> 00:00:14.178
Those tools are important, but they do not reveal every important security event automatically.

3
00:00:14.178 --> 00:00:23.378
Some threats may use legitimate tools, valid credentials, novel techniques, or low-and-slow approaches designed to blend into normal activity.

4
00:00:23.378 --> 00:00:29.394
If defenders only investigate what already triggered an alert, hidden activity may remain unnoticed.

5
00:00:29.394 --> 00:00:35.481
Threat hunting exists because defenders cannot assume that everything important will appear in an alert queue.

6
00:00:35.481 --> 00:00:42.376
Hunting is a proactive effort to search for suspicious activity that may have gone undetected by existing controls.

7
00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:50.926
A mature SOC uses alerts, investigations, incident response, detection engineering, threat intelligence, and hunting together.

8
00:00:50.926 --> 00:00:56.833
Hunting helps the team ask better questions, test assumptions, and improve visibility over time.
